{
  "_what": "What `@` offers in the message box, read from the person's own store (src/work-mentions.mjs), and what each kind looks like and does. A row reads one list: `read` is the store call (`query` its query values for a GET, `body` its body otherwise); `rows` the list in its answer; `value`, `label_field` and `detail` the fields of each row; `needs` a query value the row is read only with (the space being written in), filled into the path as {name}; `search` the query or body field the words typed after @ go in, and `search_from` how many characters must be typed before the row is read (2 when left out); `skip_when` a field that, when true, leaves a row out (the person themself). For a tool search, `read.body.search_mode: words` asks only for word-matched tools already available to this account, without run-history, meaning or registry lookup. A row names its one `kind`, or, with `kind_field`, takes each thing's kind from that field of the thing, so every kind the answer holds is offered with no row for it: such a kind must match `kind_pattern`, a kind another row names is left to that row, and it looks as parts/screen-look/show/record-kind-appearance.json says (tone as colour; its fallback, with the kind made readable, for a kind nobody styled). `source` names a row with no one kind. `wakes`: a message mentioning things of this kind is delivered only to them (they are the person's AIs). `hands_off`: in a space, a message mentioning one is also handed to it there as a job. `about`: the kind a kept message links the mention as (a kind from `kind_field` is linked as itself). `colour` is a screen-look colour id, `icon` a named icon. Where a mention opens is the screen whose `opens_kinds` (src/workspace/surfaces.json) names its kind. `native` is where the account's own owners answer that read, asked by src/native-mention-sources.mjs: `own` an operation of its own records (with `request` it carries the read's path, method and body), `shared` an operation of the space being written in, `namespace` its own Namespace resource at /namespace<path>.",
